{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1102449-is-there-an-area-for-nwod","id":1102449,"title":"Is there an area for nWoD?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-11T00:07:14-07:00","id":1102449,"title":"Is there an area for nWoD?","content":"Hi folks. Just some quick questions: is there an area for nWoD (without CoD) in this forum? If not, should I post in the CoD-part of this forum? If so, how do I find out if a topic is about either one in here? Thanks for your help in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1138-dailor","name":"dailor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T00:13:29-07:00","id":1102450,"title":"","content":"CofD is nWoD after a confusing renaming process. They are the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T01:58:36-07:00","id":1102465,"title":"","content":"The Chronicles of Darkness rebranding isn't meant to be associated with the second edition rules; those were out for a good enough while before the name rebranding. It was a licensing thing.<br /> <br /> In other words, the Chronicles of Darkness forums here are for both first and second edition nWoD, and you're welcome to post here. If you want to start a thread that specifically sticks to 1e content, just mention it in your first post. If you're not sure whether somebody is talking about first or second edition content, post and ask them. It's just folks talking, so sometimes a discussion will flow between the two, because folks are just bringing up what comes to mind from either edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T04:15:32-07:00","id":1102479,"title":"","content":"Thanks a lot.<br /> <br /> @atamajakki: sorry, as far as I can tell, they are not the same thing. First edition knows no conditions, no tilts, no beats, the defense value is much lower. ... That's why I'm asking.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar522_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"522\" data-vbnamecard=\"522\">Stupid Loserman</a> (who isn't stupid at all): thanks. That'll make it difficult for me to find my relevant threads, but I'll manage. Do you know any boards or communities dedicated to first edition nWoD? That would help me a lot. Thanks in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1138-dailor","name":"dailor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T06:16:07-07:00","id":1102489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dailor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1102449-is-there-an-area-for-nwod?p=1102479#post1102479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@atamajakki: sorry, as far as I can tell, they are not the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are. ChroD = NWoD.<br /> 1st vs 2nd Edition has nothing to do with that particular distinction.<br /> <br /> As for forums dedicated specifically to the old material, I don't know of any. As far as I'm aware, most people have moved on to second edition (some with tweaks removing the aspects they don't like).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T08:53:41-07:00","id":1102518,"title":"","content":"@Inodiv: I know what you mean and I don't want to discuss semantics here. We are on the same side: both editions are called &quot;Chronicles of Darkness&quot; now, but they don't have the same rules. They differ very much in this aspect and that is why I am looking for a place dedicated to the edition that I prefer personally.<br /> <br /> I know some groups which switched to the new CoD and some who stayed with the old material, and some who switched and switched back. But I know of no website/community who offers a place for people who prefer the old stuff. Guess I'd have to make one myself.<br /> <br /> Concerning the sites dedicated to the old material: thanks for looking. It is really appreciated. I searched, too, and didn't find such a community either.<br /> <br /> Thanks for looking, though. That's really great and helpful. You guys here are awesome!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1138-dailor","name":"dailor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T08:57:13-07:00","id":1102521,"title":"","content":"Put another way: the new White Wolf doesn't want anyone referring to anything outside of the original World of Darkness as any sort of \u201cWorld of Darkness\u201d. Onyx Path has complied with their wishes and now refer to everything that used to be called \u201cnew World of Darkness\u201d as \u201cChronicles of Darkness\u201d instead. <br /> <br /> Fans are under no obligation to respect this, and many have taken to distinguishing between 1e and 2e as \u201cnWoD\u201d and \u201cChroD\u201d because the 1e core book was called \u201cWorld of Darkness\u201d while the 2e core book is called \u201cChronicles of Darkness\u201d. But that's just fan-speak: officially, both are Chronicles of Darkness; and the forums are set up accordingly. <br /> <br /> So you're not going to see a separate nWoD section here. Besides, it would be clumsy trying to segregate 1e and 2e discussions into separate forums.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T09:14:22-07:00","id":1102529,"title":"","content":"It's pretty rare for dedicated forums to form around specific editions of games other than D&amp;D. Usually social sites are more generalized around a game as a whole, and people who want to discuss a non-current edition specify as much in their posts. D&amp;D is mostly an exception because of the massive design shifts between the TSR editions, 3.X, and 4e. Plus D&amp;D has a big enough fan base to support such subdivision. CofD is a pretty niche fandom, so separating forums for 1st and 2nd edition would leave both with very small communities. WoD might have a big enough fanbase to survive if a split occurs between fans of the classic and 20th Anniversary editions and fans of 5th edition, but we'll have to wait and see on that one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T10:52:21-07:00","id":1102561,"title":"","content":"If you want to start topics all you'll need is to add [1e] and people will understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T11:58:03-07:00","id":1102570,"title":"","content":"Thanks to everybody. This makes perfect sense. If anybody happens to stumble upon a community dedicated to 1E, I'd be glad if you'd post it here. About this particular forum here: I understood that there is no dedicated area for 1E and how to work around that. Thanks again. You are great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1138-dailor","name":"dailor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T20:20:35-07:00","id":1103001,"title":"","content":"It can be fairly confusing if you don't post 1e though, the default assumption now is that you're working with 2e for games that have it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T16:27:12-07:00","id":1103322,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1138-dailor\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1138\" data-vbnamecard=\"1138\">dailor</a> I myself vastly prefer 1e to 2e and I may be running a 1e Requiem play-by-post in the near future if you are interested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}